async () => { const s=...; for (let i=0;i<80;i++){ await sleep(100); s.player.hp=100; if(s.enemies.length && s.spawnQueue.length===0){ s.enemies.filter(e=>e.hp>0).forEach(e=>s.damageEnemy(e,9999,1)); } if(s.wave>=2) break; } return {...}; }
```
But if we kill enemies as they spawn while queue not empty, queue keeps spawning but eventually empties; need also kill new ones. Loop each 100ms kills all alive; eventually queue empties and all dead -> clear -> wave 2. This works. Set player invuln perhaps. Also s.player.hp=100 each tick. We can kill before they attack. It will take ~? queue 3 enemies spawn every 1-1.45s after banner 2.8s: ~7s. Fine. 100 iterations 10s; max. Let's do 120 iterations and break at wave 2. Use async eval.

