Could rotate the gameplay 90°? No.

Maybe use portrait layout with the game at top (y 60) and touch controls immediately below (y 300), leaving bottom empty but thumbs could rest at screen bottom? Not.

I think it's acceptable for a 16:9 game on portrait. But we can use the empty screen space for a decorative background and maybe instructions ("GIRE PARA TELA CHEIA"). The stage background is dark with radial gradient; blank but stylish. The controls at bottom separated. Not too bad. The pause button at top right is far from frame (y 8, frame 250) making it look disconnected. Move pause button relative to frame? The fixed pause at top is above the frame far. Could place pause button just below frame top? Or make it inside the canvas HUD (tappable). The empty top is weird. Since frame centered, the pause button floats at top. Better to add a touch pause action in the canvas HUD and hide the fixed button in portrait? Or position fixed button at top of frame dynamically via style. We can update on resize: `pauseBtn.style.top = ...` based on frame rect. Or place pause button inside the touch controls area (near the actions) rather than top fixed. Simpler: move the pause button in CSS into the bottom controls? The bottom center has gap between D-pad and actions. A pause button fixed bottom center could work. Or add it to the action group. But then touch layout: pad left; actions right; could add pause at top center. Better: move pause top-right position to follow the game frame. In App.resize: 
