All waves completed, victory. But `enemies:1` at victory because pendingVictory triggered when boss died with one add still alive. That's the design issue: victory while one enemy remains. Could be a bit odd: the victory screen shows an enemy still in the arena (frozen) behind the overlay. Could fix by requiring all enemies dead OR making remaining adds die when boss dies. Better: On boss death, trigger a "boss death" that kills/knocks out all remaining enemies? Or don't trigger victory until all enemies dead. Since wave 5 spawn queue includes adds that may spawn after boss death, requiring all dead means you might fight adds after boss; that's fine. But the current `pendingVictory` triggers 1.4s. Simpler: in `killEnemy` for minotaur, set `pendingVictory` only if no other living enemies? But spawnQueue may still have adds; if we kill boss before adds spawn, updateWave will continue spawning and eventually clear; set pendingVictory? It would still fire 1.4s later. Could set `pendingVictory` only when the wave is clear. The wave clear block handles wave 5 → victory. The boss kill triggers `waveState`? updateWave will see spawnQueue maybe empty and enemies all dead after deathT; then clear and victory. That's robust. Remove pendingVictory entirely or set it only if the arena is otherwise empty. But the current flow with other adds: boss dies, adds remain, pendingVictory fires 1.4s regardless; not good.

Better design: On minotaur death, don't set pendingVictory; let the normal wave-clear flow finish the remaining adds, then victory after clear timer. This requires player to defeat remaining adds, which is fine. Wave 5 spawns 5 enemies total; the boss is first plus 4 adds. After boss dies, up to 3 adds may remain. Fighting them after the boss is anticlimactic; the victory should maybe happen after boss. Alternative: on boss death, instantly kill all remaining enemies (they "flee/die") and clear spawn queue, so the arena goes clear and victory plays. That is dramatic and prevents leftover. In killEnemy minotaur:
```
for (const other of this.enemies) if (other!==e && other.hp>0) { other.hp=0; other.state='dying'; ... } 
this.spawnQueue.length=0;
this.pendingVictory=1.4;
```
But then kills/score? Could count as kills; but visually adds dissolve. Or simply in `victory()` clear enemies/spawnQueue; the victory overlay covers. But `enemies:1` remains rendered behind overlay; could freeze but visually no issue once overlay dims. Yet the wave state 'fight' at victory means update stops; still one alive. It's not ideal but not fatal. Better to clear adds at victory:
```
victory() {
  ...
  this.spawnQueue.length = 0;
  for (const e of this.enemies) { if (e.hp>0) { e.hp=0; e.state='dying'; e.deathT=0; } }
  this.enemies = [];
